# Flutter + Riverpod Fast UI Development Rules

## Objective

Prioritize **speed**, **consistency**, and **scalability** for building multiple UI screens quickly. Avoid over-engineering while keeping code clean and production-ready.

---

## Package usage

Prefer current stable versions of: `flutter_riverpod`, `hooks_riverpod`, `go_router`, `freezed`, `json_serializable`, `dio`, `flutter_screenutil`, `intl`.

Run **build_runner** after adding or changing **freezed** / **json_serializable** models.

---

## Project architecture

**Feature-first**: feature code lives under `lib/page/<feature_name>/` with `widget/` for page-only UI.

Shared layers:

```text
lib/
├── core/
├── router/
├── service/
├── theme/
├── widget/
└── page/
```

All app code stays under `lib/`.

---

## Page structure

Each screen lives in `lib/page/<feature_name>/`, for example:

- `home_page.dart`, `home_provider.dart`, `home_state.dart`, `home_repository.dart`, `home_model.dart`, `widget/`

Page-specific widgets **must** stay in that feature’s `widget/` folder.

---

## File size (100 lines)

- **Target:** each **hand-written** Dart file **≤ ~100 lines** when practical.
- **If larger:** split into extra files or a subfolder (same feature).
- **Exceptions (do not split by line count alone):**
  - Generated code (`lib/l10n/app_localizations*.dart`, build outputs).
  - Large **theme / typography** facades — refactor via **planned** API splits (tokens, namespaces), not only line chopping.
- See `.cursor/commands/refactor.md` for how to apply this in refactors.

Other style: prefer `const`, trailing commas, arrow syntax for tiny methods, avoid nested ternaries, prefer `final`, avoid magic numbers (use theme/constants).

---

## SOLID

- Prefer **composition** over deep inheritance.
- Keep **UI**, **state**, and **data/network** concerns separated.

---

## Riverpod

- **Declare** providers at **top level** or in `*_provider.dart` — **not** as nested classes inside widgets.
- **Naming:** `*Provider` (e.g. `homeProvider`, `visitorDetailProvider`).
- **Sync state:** `Notifier` / `NotifierProvider` where appropriate.
- **Async / API:** `FutureProvider`, `AsyncNotifier`, or `FutureProvider.family` — use what fits the feature.
- **Scope:** page/feature providers stay under that feature folder; avoid unnecessary globals.
- **Providers** must not contain **UI** code (no `BuildContext`, no widgets).
- **Using** `ref.watch` / `ref.read` in **`ConsumerWidget`** / **`Consumer`** is **allowed** — that is not “defining providers inside widgets.”

---

## UI rules

- **Widgets** must not **perform HTTP** or **own** business rules (validation rules live in helpers/notifiers/repositories).
- **No hardcoded** colors, font sizes, padding, or radii — use **theme** (`app_text_style`, `app_color`, `app_spacing`, `app_radius`, etc.).
- **Loading overlays:** prefer `lib/widget/modal_progress_hud.dart` for **full-screen** or **page-level** blocking loads. **Small** inline loaders (e.g. inside a **dialog**, **button**, or **list tile**) may use `CircularProgressIndicator` when a full-screen HUD would be wrong UX.

---

## Theme system

Centralize styling under `lib/theme/` (`app_color.dart`, `app_text_style.dart`, `app_spacing.dart`, `app_radius.dart`, typography subfolders as needed). **All** screen styling should go through these (and `AppTheme` extensions where used).

---

## Responsiveness

Use **flutter_screenutil** for responsive units: `.w`, `.h`, `.sp`, `.r`. Layouts should work on **phone and tablet**.

---

## Navigation

- Use **go_router** only (no `Navigator.push` for app navigation).
- **Route table** is **composed** under `lib/router/` (e.g. `app_router.dart` entry + `app_route.dart` + route builder modules). New routes belong in the router **folder**, not necessarily in a single monolithic file.

---

## API layer

- **Dio** is configured via **`lib/service/api_service.dart`** (`dioProvider`, shared options/headers).
- **HTTP calls** live in **repositories** (e.g. `*_repository.dart` next to the feature), using **Dio** from `dioProvider` and **auth token** from `authRepositoryProvider` / storage — **not** raw `http` from widgets.
- Repositories **map** JSON/DTOs to **domain/UI models**; **widgets** do not parse JSON.

---

## Models

- **Prefer** **freezed** + **json_serializable** for non-trivial domain models and shared DTOs.
- **Lightweight API DTOs** may use **manual** `factory fromJson` when codegen is not justified — still **immutable** fields, map to UI models before display.
- **Do not** pass raw DTOs to widgets when a dedicated UI model exists.

---

## Error handling

- Prefer handling errors in **notifiers / repositories / providers**; keep widgets thin.
- **Result / Success / Failure** patterns are encouraged for new flows where they improve clarity; existing code may use **throw** / **AsyncValue.error** — stay consistent within a feature.

---

## Logging

Use `dart:developer` **`log()`** — avoid `print()` in production code paths.

---

## Reusable widgets

Shared building blocks live under `lib/widget/` (e.g. `app_button.dart`, `app_text_field.dart`, `modal_progress_hud.dart`). Feature-only widgets stay under `lib/page/<feature>/widget/`.

---

## Naming

| Kind    | Example        |
|---------|----------------|
| Page    | `HomePage`     |
| Provider| `homeProvider` |
| State   | `HomeState`    |
| Repo    | `HomeRepository` |
| Model   | `HomeModel`    |
| Shared widget | `AppButton` |

---

## Linting

Enable **flutter_lints**. Avoid `dynamic`, unnecessary `late`, and needless nullability.

---

## Restrictions (summary)

- No **business rules** in dumb widgets; no **direct API** from widgets.
- No **provider class definitions** inside widget class bodies.
- No **hardcoded** styling outside theme.
- No **DTOs** as the primary data type in UI — map to UI/domain models.
- No **`Navigator.push`** for app routes.
- **Prefer** ≤100 lines per hand-written file; use exceptions above.

---

## Environment

- Environments: **staging** (`main_dev.dart`, Android flavor `dev`) / **production** (`main_prod.dart`, flavor `prod`). See `docs/BUILD_APK.md`.
- Secrets: `.env` or `--dart-define` — never commit keys.

---

## Fonts & typography

- Use **Manrope** via centralized text styles (see `lib/theme/` typography).
- **Do not** hardcode `fontSize` or `fontFamily` in random widgets — use **`app_text_style.dart`** (and related typography files) with `.sp` where applicable.
- Standard scale (reference): title **18.sp**, subtitle **16.sp**, body **14.sp** — apply through theme APIs, not literals in widgets.

---

## Deliverables mindset

- Clear feature folders, `pubspec.yaml` + codegen where needed, tests for critical paths, analyzer-clean changes.
